\e[2J\e[1;1HTest SGR-0 color reset\r\r\n
\r\r\n
ECMA-48 states that SGR 0 "cancels the effect of any preceding occurrence\r\r\n
of SGR in the data stream regardless of the setting of the graphic rendition\r\r\n
combination mode (GRCM)".\r\r\n
\r\r\n
\r\r\n
\e[0;40;37;39;49m\e[0mYou should see only black:\e[30;40mSGR 30 and SGR 40 don't work\e[0;40;37;39;49m
\e[0m:up to here\r\r\n
\e[0;40;37;39;49m\e[0mYou should see only white:\e[37;47mSGR 37 and SGR 47 don't work\e[0;40;37;39;49m
\e[0m:up to here\r\r\n
\e[0;40;37;39;49m\e[0mYou should see text here: \e[30;40m\e[0mSGR 0 reset works (explicit 0)\r\r\n
\e[0;40;37;39;49m\e[0m................and here: \e[37;47m\e[mSGR 0 reset works (default param)\r\r\n
\e[0;40;37;39;49m\e[0mPush <RETURN>
